HELM CHARTS - DEVOPS ENGINEER WORKFLOW

Step 1: Verify Helm Installation at the Machine level(Agent node) where execute the kubernetes is installed

wget https://get.helm.sh/helm-v3.18.6-linux-amd64.tar.gz
tar -xzf helm-v3.18.6-linux-amd64.tar.gz
sudo mv linux-amd64/helm /usr/local/bin/

helm version

Step 2: Add Helm Repository (Example: Bitnami)
"A Helm repository stores Helm charts, just like Docker Hub stores Docker images.
We use helm repo add to add a repository to our local Helm client so that we can search, download, and install pre-built applications like NGINX, MySQL, Redis, and Jenkins using Helm.

helm repo add bitnami https://charts.bitnami.com/bitnami  

Step 3: Update Helm Repository
helm repo update

Step 4: Search Available Charts
helm search repo nginx
helm search repo mysql

helm install my-nginx bitnami/nginx

Step 5: Create a New Helm Chart
helm create myapp

This creates the following structure:

myapp/
├── Chart.yaml
├── values.yaml
├── charts/
├── templates/
│   ├── deployment.yaml
│   ├── service.yaml
│   ├── ingress.yaml
│   ├── serviceaccount.yaml
│   ├── hpa.yaml
│   └── _helpers.tpl

Step 6: Modify values.yaml

Example:
replicaCount: 2

image:
  repository: loksaieta/bankingwebapp
  tag: latest

service:
  type: ClusterIP
  port: 8080

Step 7: Modify templates if required

deployment.yaml
service.yaml
ingress.yaml
configmap.yaml
secret.yaml

Step 8: Validate Helm Chart

helm lint myapp

Step 9: Generate Kubernetes YAML

helm template myapp

Step 10: Install Helm Chart

helm install banking-app ./myapp

Step 11: Verify Installation

helm list

kubectl get all

Step 12: Upgrade Application

helm upgrade banking-app ./myapp

Step 13: Check Release Status

helm status banking-app

Step 14: View Release History

helm history banking-app

Step 15: Rollback

helm rollback banking-app 1

Step 16: Uninstall

helm uninstall banking-app

Useful Commands:

